{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/246393-fairy-tales-and-ghost-stories-shared-likenesses-of-fae-and-the-dead","id":246393,"title":"Fairy Tales and Ghost Stories - Shared Likenesses of Fae and the Dead","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-01T15:45:56-07:00","id":246393,"title":"Fairy Tales and Ghost Stories - Shared Likenesses of Fae and the Dead","content":"Lacking the mental energy to arrange these into discrete paragraphs, found below is a bulleted list of some observations of similarities I've accumulated in the course of reading Changeling, Geist, and other instances of ghosts throughout the WoD.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Glamour stemming from both emotion and supernatural bonds/bindings - anchors provide Essence and can be either things that emotionally resonate with the ghost or things that some supernatural agency have bound it to (ostensibly under the same clause that gives some anchors the subtag of &quot;unfinished business&quot;).<br /> \u2022 The Underworld and the Hedge both utilize portals as their primary means of entrance and egress, in contrast to the Shadow and the Astral's more typical &quot;change of perspective&quot; mechanisms.<br /> \u2022 Trods, for what little mention their Earthside manifestations have received, are framed as founts of Glamour - an open Avernian Gate gives ghosts within its proximity enough Essence to last the scene without being drawn back inside.<br /> \u2022 Mirrors and false images as a stock in trade.<br /> \u2022 Book of the Dead posits a strange predilection among the dead for games - chess with Death, etc?<br /> \u2022 The sometime consequences of bringing a person back from the Underworld resonate with the subtle differences between a fetch and its basis.<br /> \u2022 Mazes and labyrinths between gods and men.<br /> \u2022 Cruel and exacting gods who deal in &quot;equivalent&quot; exchange, often of the bizarre or terrible variety.<br /> \u2022 A predilection toward enslavement of &quot;lesser&quot; beings, including mortals.<br /> \u2022 Powerful passions and emotions as a means of staving off fading out of sentience.<br /> \u2022 Described impact of Fae Dwindling similar to examples of ghosts without emotional or supernatural investment.<br /> \u2022 The effects of disuse upon regions of Faerie are that the place takes on an aspect of death and decay - the Underworld's denizens bear their deathmarks more overtly than their anchored cousins.<br /> \u2022 Gravewights and burial mounds and Maya Sharptongue's point of egress.<br /> \u2022 The Grave Dream, <i>Et in Arcadia ego.</i><br /> \u2022 One mythic origin of the Nosferatu in their clanbook says they became what they are (rather than just vampires) by consumption of the essence of the beings in the Underworld; the same book includes a changeling calling one of the Dragons his &quot;second Keeper&quot; and makes note of Nosferatu feeding habits including the draining of blood from sleeping persons.<br /> <br /> There are almost certainly others. Anyone care to note them or comment upon the above list?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T09:45:10-08:00","id":301194,"title":"","content":"A latecomer or three:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Keepers and Kerberoi weaker nearer to the mortal realm.<br /> \u2022 Formation of a Court or krewe giving founders a free dot of Mantle/Status, irrevocably tying them to the group, and removing some degree of free will through the involvement of fate.<br /> \u2022 Ruled By Passion and Vice Addiction/2e ghost WP recovery mechanics.<br /> \u2022 Gentry and the Kerberoi as extensions of their domains.<br /> \u2022 Definite or theoretical use of intruding supernaturals as a means of expansion (Becoming Nightmare and the Kerberoi-as-former-Sin-Eaters theory).<br /> \u2022 Briarwolves and the posited pedigree of some of the guardians of Tartarus.<br /> \u2022 Explicit ontological ambiguity of Fae and Kerberos.<br /> \u2022 Existence of an overt threshold between deep Hedge and Arcadia loosely analogous to the first river of the Underworld separating Erebus from Tartarus (explicit example of a threshold guardian to the Fae is a Cerberus).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T11:16:14-08:00","id":301314,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of very good reasons I like Geist. It's mirroring of Changeling contributes heartily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T12:21:18-08:00","id":301410,"title":"","content":"I remember one of those speculations on nature of supernaturals from viewpoint of Changelings in one of Changeling books which suggested supernaturals associated with death such as vampires (Geist was not released at that people) might be people taken to the underworld who escaped back which implied there could be equivalents of Keepers there. Authors tried to draw some comparisons long before Geist, and this light mirroring Changeling in certain aspects could be intentional. Only sad thing it did not mirror Changeling's length as a line <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T13:07:34-08:00","id":301455,"title":"","content":"I'm almost certain that the similarities between the Lost and some varieties of Kindred in terms of direct ties to types of Old God that &quot;shouldn't be around anymore&quot; are a deliberate part of the metaphysics. Which reminds me of an obvious one:<br /> <br /> \u2022 The story of the Unholy and the Old Hag bears a loose similarity to a Durance. (&quot;True monsters are made with great effort and care.&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T11:36:02-08:00","id":302475,"title":"","content":"You know, I read on local folklore and the line between ghosts and nature spirits/fae is very blurry. Our brand of Changelings is taken captive by ghosts and when they return back they exhibit minor physical changes and major changes in personality from the experience. Actually, I had a classmate who came to believe she was a Changeling after her personality started shifting in disturbing for her and us ways. She believed she was taken by a ghost which she slighted by accident and that she somehow made it back.<br /> <br /> Also one metal band I listen to that bases its album concepts on Ugrofinnic folklore also exhibits that motive of people being kidnapped by spirits of underworld.<br /> <br /> Anyway, time to research local folklore further for Slavic mythology stuff, but actually assigning a splat to a certain type of creatures might prove difficult. Is Leszy a nature spirit, True Fae, hobgoblin, changeling or a werewolf? Nobody can be sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 11-04-2014, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T12:41:21-08:00","id":302543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/246393-fairy-tales-and-ghost-stories-shared-likenesses-of-fae-and-the-dead?p=302475#post302475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Leszy a nature spirit, True Fae, hobgoblin, changeling or a werewolf? Nobody can be sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that easily we can assume he is True Fae being...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wikipedia about Leszy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Leshy protects the animals and birds in the forest and tells them when to migrate. He can </span></span></span>shapeshift<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> into many different forms. As a human, he looks like a peasant with glowing eyes, and his shoes are on backwards.</span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A person who befriends a leshy can learn the secrets of magic. Farmers and shepherds would make pacts with the leshy to protect their crops and sheep. The leshy has many tricks, including leading peasants astray, making them sick, or tickling them to death. They are also known to hide the axes of woodcutters. A person gets lost in the woods when a leshy crosses their path. To find the way out, you have to turn your clothes inside out and wear shoes on opposite feet.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Leshies are terribly mischievous beings: they have horrible cries, and can imitate voices of people familiar to wanderers and lure them back to their caves, where the leshies will tickle them to death; they also remove signs from their posts. Leshies aren't evil: although they enjoy misguiding humans and kidnapping young women, they are also known to keep grazing cattle from wandering too far into the forests and getting lost. Sometimes cow herders will make pacts with a leshy by handing him their crosses from around their necks and sharing communion with him after Christian church gatherings; these pacts are said to give the cowherds special powers.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sometimes more than one leshy inhabits a forest, and then they will fight for their territory, knocking down trees and scaring animals. It is believed that the cries of Eurasian bitterns were once thought to be the Leshy's snore, as he was also linked to the swamp and the marshes. Similar accounts were also made for the Vodyanoy.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-04-2014, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T13:03:36-08:00","id":303658,"title":"","content":"It's not that only True Fae were interested in women. Zmeis did too, and given they impregnated women they had a creative spark.<br /> <br /> I'm actually making a faction of a Conspiracy that harbors a lineage hailing from Zmeis, but they are not organized enough like Lucifuge to have their own Conspiracy. They share one Conspiracy with 2 other factions that include sorcerors following footsteps of Twardowski i S\u0119dziw\u00f3j who use alchemy, divination and necromancy for both upholding Vigil and increasing their wealth (they bankroll many operations) and another whose first leader was a pre-Christian craftsmen who slayed a beast plaguing a freehold through trickery and freed ruler of another freehold from Keeper who took him back, forging pacts of mutual alliance between his apprentices and local Changelings. Passed their knowledge orally within organizations of craftsmen and guilds, now they mingle with local communities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T22:52:24-08:00","id":315955,"title":"","content":"Another one, courtesy of Midnight Roads:<br /> <br /> \u2022 The End of the Road is theorized to be <i>an</i> (if not necessarily <i>the</i>) Underworld and effectively turns the player characters from living to dead without the intervening step of actually dying; its guiding intelligence is described as inherently mean-spirited and childlike, it &quot;dimly and instinctively craves stimulation, a feeling of belonging and participation in something greater than itself,&quot; creates flawed doppelg\u00e4ngers of the PCs, is capable of retrieving the characters from their escape attempts &quot;as though they walked away in a dream and [woke] up in the exact spot in which they fell asleep,&quot; and causes anything in the scene that isn't a player character or a doppelganger thereof to gradually begin to look decayed or degraded when the PCs aren't paying attention to them.<br /> <br /> Which in turn reminds me of a couple more:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Primacy of Vice in associated metaphysics (2e ghost Willpower recovery, Ruled By Passion, Vice addiction, Vice as Hedge Key, etc).<br /> \u2022 Raised possibility of multiple Underworlds (<i>Vampire: Mythologies</i>, <i>Midnight Roads</i>) and multiple Faeries (<i>Equinox Road</i>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T13:11:29-08:00","id":316473,"title":"","content":"These are some really interesting connections! Even more so since real-world fairly tales and ghost stories often have a lot of overlap: the transformative brush with the supernatural, a moral aspect (eg, &quot;bad things will happen to you if you disobey your parents, mistreat your wife, etc&quot;), strange rules that shouldn't be broken, but often are anyway (&quot;Do not laugh as the hearse goes by&quot; comes to mind). Is there anything you were planning on doing with these connections?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T14:19:48-08:00","id":316527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/246393-fairy-tales-and-ghost-stories-shared-likenesses-of-fae-and-the-dead?p=316473#post316473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are some really interesting connections! Even more so since real-world fairly tales and ghost stories often have a lot of overlap: the transformative brush with the supernatural, a moral aspect (eg, &quot;bad things will happen to you if you disobey your parents, mistreat your wife, etc&quot;), strange rules that shouldn't be broken, but often are anyway (&quot;Do not laugh as the hearse goes by&quot; comes to mind). Is there anything you were planning on doing with these connections?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly I just made this thread as a collection ground since a couple months ago it became readily apparent that my primary method of highlighting these sorts of connections is not terribly secure against accidental total deletion.<br /> <br /> A more esoteric one:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Mummy's <i>Guildhalls of the Deathless</i> chapter on the Mesen-Nebu (i.e. the alchemists' guild) talks about how alchemy is <i>payment</i>, and the sidebar on the Subtle Bazaar mentions how after the 10th century writings on the supposed allegory reference it as though it were a literal place, managed by jinn, trading strange things and running the risk of getting what they wanted with a nasty twist if their bargain was bad. Geist's four Elemental Keys explicitly draw from alchemical symbolism and share a Key Skill with the powertype revolving around one of the most basic kinds of supernatural prices (as the vampires know Damned well), to say nothing of the earlier mentioned chthonic equivalent-exchange laws.<br /> <br /> Mummy's corebook section on the alchemists also talks about a curiosity of the force their alchemy manipulates:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The lords of Irem made one house out of its smiths, jewelers, and mine overseers. The Shan\u2019iatu revealed that they all unlocked the alchemical essence: Dedwen, or \u201cprosperity.\u201d Modern philosophers might call Dedwen \u201cutility\u201d because it symbolizes <b>an occult principle of value that transcends particular applications.</b> The alchemists knew that all material creation harvested Dedwen and urged it toward a particular manifestation.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> <b>The alchemists suffer from a weakness for beauty, for it is the most enigmatic form of Dedwen.</b> Material strength, wealth, and political prestige have straightforward uses. Esthetic properties are powerful for reasons that lie at the edge of the alchemists\u2019 understanding. [\u2026] One Born of Gold also appreciates the beauty of skillful actions. An archer striking her mark creates Dedwen in excellence. It is said that high alchemy manipulates esthetic value along with material properties\u2014that in sacrifice, a beautiful servant or great swordsman makes a blade sharper. </div> </div> </div>Cut back to Changeling, and\u2026<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Introduction: A Game of Beautiful Madness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Faerie is beautiful. It isn\u2019t kindly, or nurturing or benevolent, but it is wondrously beautiful.</b> The same is true for its children, both those who were born of its unreal matter and those mortals who were abducted and nursed on its magic. Even a hideous Ogre may have some strangely sketched artistry to its asymmetrical features, and even a Darkling of disturbing mien may have an elegantly hypnotic grace or cold, frank sexuality. But as the Lost move among the mortal world, trying to recover their old lives or draw enough Glamour to sustain themselves, they become aware of the beautiful things that mortals often take for granted. To a changeling, there is beauty in the grief hanging over the funeral of a good man, or in the awkward way a young girl twists her hands at a school dance. They see things nobody else does \u2014 not simply because they can, but because they try.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chapter 4: Storytelling</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Beauty can come from the strangest places, or things that don\u2019t normally suggest beauty can in fact become beautiful in their function.</b> Consider the savage beauty of a shark or lion, for example, and recall the \u201cterrible\u201d beauty of the witch-queen Jadis from The Chronicles of Narnia. Think about the beauty of loss \u2014 a virtuoso composition of a dirge, a masterfully painted memorial of a hero long gone, the turning of the leaves in autumn before the dead season. Recall a significant break-up: It was hell to go through, but aren\u2019t you glad she\u2019s gone now?</div> </div> </div> </div>The diversity of resources the fae can draw upon and ask for is always a fun balancing act to contemplate, I think.<br /> <br /> And while we're on the subject of similarities not specific to the World of Darkness\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2022 &quot;Don't speak ill of the dead&quot; is curiously similar in practice to the conventions of not calling the fae by unflattering names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T12:00:09-08:00","id":317606,"title":"","content":"I wonder what would happen if a Fae managed to change its &quot;hardware&quot; to run the Underworld and Hedge &quot;Software&quot; simultaneously. Not to mention that a Dead Dominion and a Keeper's realm bear a number of things in common, and let us consider how closely entwined death and dreams are...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":". 11-20-2014, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T20:21:46-08:00","id":317892,"title":"","content":"One might also note the tendency for both the Fae and Geists to go by evocative monikers. The Queen of Glass. The Skull Gambler. And so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T06:32:47-08:00","id":318208,"title":"","content":"Or that mythology never could make up its mind weather the Wild Hunt was made up of ghosts or fae. Heck, in Welsh myths, the head rider is god of the Dead AND lord of the Fae...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T12:52:22-08:00","id":319193,"title":"","content":"That is true yes. Plus, there's that whole thing in Celtic mythology about the Fair Folk living underground...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T13:48:19-08:00","id":329525,"title":"","content":"Fresh one from rereading Autumn Nightmares:<br /> \u2022 The inability of Charlatans/anchored ghosts to enter the Hedge/the Underworld, and the motivations of both are focused around those things keeping them in the world of mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-03-2014, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T12:17:10-08:00","id":331380,"title":"","content":"Harkening back tot he other real world examples - in Finnish myth fairy and ghost usually mean the same thing. The Irish obviously make the cross-over with banshees. If you do enough research on wikipedia, you can find a whole discourse on wether or not fae and dead are synonymous in different cultures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4297-explodingjoe","name":"ExplodingJoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T12:29:17-07:00","id":513229,"title":"","content":"Also from Autumn Nightmares, upon review:<br /> \u2022 Fae becoming more humanlike Charlatans as a result of either death in the right context or forming a connection with a human has parallels with the Bargain's general vectors and its necessity for a geist destroyed in the Underworld to continue existence as an incarnate being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T18:17:48-07:00","id":513555,"title":"","content":"I believe some traditions (I want to say Celtic and Scottish, but don't quote me on that) view the fairy world and the afterlife as the same thing. Therefore at least some fairy creatures might very well be akin to ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T18:33:39-07:00","id":513570,"title":"","content":"Yeah. That's one of three reasons I tend to speak of faerie tales with connotations to journeys to the underworld, particularly Orpheus.<br /> <br /> The other two being by subtle recognition of similarities brought into the foreground by Satchel and Kyle Kallgren's review of La Belle et La Bete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T05:07:39-07:00","id":514040,"title":"","content":"And 9 laws of Grave Dream? Specifically don't bring cold iron and don't speak of Cousins..Then there is legend that true Fae made Contract with Death, and that terms can be learned in Underworld...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T06:52:12-07:00","id":514084,"title":"","content":"Broaden your view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T07:34:23-07:00","id":514103,"title":"","content":"Changeling has a fairly common spider motif going on (Venombites, Harvestmen, Pattern Eaters, Marquise Tistresse, that one recurring changeling in the artwork with a large spider protruding out of her forehead), while <i>Book of the Dead</i>'s opening fiction includes an arachnoid Kerberos, and later the book discusses a giant ghost-eating spider hiding within the Hagia Sophia's Avernian gate. Throw in the Azlu and spiders in the World of Darkness seem to be quintessential threshold-tenders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T07:14:49-07:00","id":515122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/246393-fairy-tales-and-ghost-stories-shared-likenesses-of-fae-and-the-dead?p=514084#post514084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Broaden your view.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was quite a long since I read Geist the Sin eater, so I don't remember much about it in terms of setting.. but I do remember that thing I loved about it is same as in Changeling-a)PC has encounter with something strange and alien, and comes back changed, and balance those lives,b) doesn't quite belong neither within Underworld or our world ( Sin Eaters), or within mortal world or Arcadia ( Changelings),c) Geists and Sin-Eaters both inhabit one body, changeling sometimes develops dual personality-one for it's human side and other for fae side,d) power of both come from bargain,e) more powerful they grow, more they fall to inhuman side ( changelings become capricious and Clarity sometimes drops, Geist and Sin-Eater more act as one mind).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T01:16:35-07:00","id":524165,"title":"","content":"This is a really interesting thread! As other people have said, the folklores these things originate from often didn't treat them as fundamentally separate categories in the way supernatural fantasy authors in the 21st century like to have fae courts versus vampire domains versus ghost-haunted revenants as distinct things. I would take that a bit further and suggest that what's happening here is that authors are sometimes taking their inspiration ultimately from the same ideas and casting them as different things depending on their specific gameline- the idea of a portal to another world is being used as both Hedge gates and Avernian ones, for example.<br /> <br /> One that i've thought about before: consider how many supernatural types are created by dying (sometimes metaphorically) and coming back to life changed. Your comparison of fetches to &quot;came back wrong&quot; revenants is really good for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}